WEBVTT

00:02:56.964 --> 00:03:01.219
They learned to cultivate olives,
vines and date palms.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.972
They invented leavened bread, beer,

00:03:04.972 --> 00:03:07.099
and they developed textile technologies:

00:03:07.099 --> 00:03:09.352
the potter's wheel, the sail.

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:13.105
And they spread all of these
innovations far and wide,

00:03:13.105 --> 00:03:15.858
from the shores
of the eastern Mediterranean,

00:03:15.858 --> 00:03:17.443
up to the Black Sea,

00:03:17.443 --> 00:03:19.487
and from the Persian Gulf,

00:03:19.487 --> 00:03:24.200
all the way over
to the mountains of Kurdistan,

00:03:24.242 --> 00:03:27.828
where our excavations were taking place.

00:03:28.704 --> 00:03:33.334
I've often referred, half jokingly,
to this long period of human history